;; Every waymark10/src file that reads a factory kind (ticket, change,
;; ci_run, repo_policy) or a dwelling kind (self, journal, letter) by
;; name, with its count of such reads the day scripts/core-tier-check.sh
;; landed (core tier, slice 1; docs/core-tiers.md). How a read is
;; recognised is written in that script. A count may only go down, and
;; its entry should follow it down; a file that reaches zero leaves the
;; list. Add no new entry: ask the module through a hook
;; (waymark10.modules.hooks) instead.
{"waymark10/src/waymark10/server/judgments.clj" 1
 "waymark10/src/waymark10/server/live_cracks.clj" 2
 "waymark10/src/waymark10/server/org.clj" 1
 "waymark10/src/waymark10/server/promises.clj" 1}
